 * validator treats a single-value and a multi-value column identically at the
 * group-by boundary, so a build may emit a group-by over a multi-value column
 * with nothing in the stack able to say what the page then shows. The two
 * candidate behaviours are not variants of one another. A file listed under
 * EVERY value it holds makes the group counts add up to more than the file
 * count; a file listed once under a joined label makes one group per distinct
 * SET. A rule cannot be written for either until one of them is measured.
 *
 * WHAT IT ASKS. Ids follow the grammar in `test/manual/SURFACES.md`,
 * `<surface>.<scope>.<question>`. Every measurement is about how a document
 * library's view diverges from a generic list's, so they file under
