// finding: library-grouping-a-group-by-is-never-refused - the first live run,
// 2026-09-08, sent a <GroupBy> naming a column that does not exist and got HTTP
// 200 back with flat rows. A negative control asserting a REFUSAL therefore
// failed on a probe that was working, and voided six measurements that had been
// made. The discriminator a group-by needs is not refused against accepted but
// HONOURED against IGNORED: an honoured group-by returns group rows, fewer than
// the files, each carrying the grouping markers `<Field>.COUNT.group`,
// `<Field>.newgroup` and `<Field>.groupindex` that the positive control
// recorded on GroupChoice in that run; an ignored one returns the flat rows.
// The control measures the flat shape in the same run rather than assuming it
// is one row per file, by sending the same query twice and varying only the
// <GroupBy>.
// finding: library-grouping-a-collapsed-row-carries-no-file-name - the second
// live run, 2026-09-08, sent the missing-column <GroupBy> with ViewFields
// naming FileLeafRef and got four rows back that did not carry it, the first
// being `{"PreviewThumbnailsQualitySets":""}`. A count of rows per file over
// those rows is therefore undefined for every file, and the negative control,
// which required one row per file, reported NOT ESTABLISHED against clean data
// and voided six measurements a second time. The flat signature is decided by
// the row count against the same query sent with no <GroupBy>, and by the
// absence of the grouping markers; the per-file count is evidence only.
// finding: library-grouping-client-side-partition-is-not-evidence - a probe
// that sends a grouped query, gets flat rows back and sorts them into buckets
// by reading each row's value has measured its own arithmetic. The rows would
// partition the same way with no <GroupBy> in the query at all, so the method
// cannot separate a grouping SharePoint performed from one it ignored. The two
// observations used here are both server-produced: the COLLAPSED query's group
// rows (their count, their labels, the keys they carry), and the EXPANDED
// query's row count against a file count this probe knows because it uploaded
// the files. A file returned on more rows than it has is the server splitting
// it, and nothing else can produce that.
// finding: library-grouping-fixture-must-be-acyclic - the library holds a
// lookup into the target list, so the target list cannot be recycled while the
// library exists. `multilookup-probe.js` records SharePoint refusing to recycle
// a list another list's lookup points into, and `cross-lookup-probe.js` carries
// the same finding. CLEANUP here removes the library before the target for
// that reason, and the header tells the operator the same order.
// finding: library-grouping-multi-value-write-shape-is-list-measured - the item
// payload a multi-value column takes was measured on a generic LIST, not on a
// library: `{"__metadata": {"type": "Collection(Edm.String)"}, "results": [..]}`
