// `{"<Name>Id": {"results": [..]}}` for a multi-value lookup
// (multilookup-probe.js, 2026-09-02), both quoted in analysis/typemap.py. A
// library reaches its rows through `items(id)` and is not the container either
// run used, so the shape is tried as an ordered experiment rather than assumed:
// the two nometadata shapes library-column-interactions-probe.js sends on a
// library first, then the verbose list-measured shape. The fixture row reports
// which one took, and a shape that returns HTTP 200 without reading back is not
// counted as one that took.
// finding: library-grouping-lookup-direction-is-library-to-list - the lookup
// columns here are held BY the library and point AT a list, never the reverse.
// `cross-lookup-probe.js` measured on 2026-09-07 that a list's lookup into a
// library binds but its value cannot be SET through the item MERGE (HTTP 500,
// file target and folder target alike), while the library-to-list direction's
// item write held in the same run. A fixture built the other way round would
